The [[Wicked: The Soundtrack|films' soundtracks]] were co-billed to Grande, who performed several songs from the musical and an original track titled "[[The Girl in the Bubble]]", written by [[Stephen Schwartz]] for the [[Wicked: For Good – The Soundtrack|''Wicked: For Good'' soundtrack]].<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Comiter |first=Jordana |date=November 22, 2025 |title=''Wicked: For Good''{{'}}s 2 New Songs: Everything to Know About the Original Tracks Sung by Cynthia Erivo and Ariana Grande |url=https://people.com/wicked-for-good-new-songs-what-to-know-11853864 |access-date=November 22, 2025 |magazine=[[People (magazine)|People]]}}
* {{cite magazine |last=Cremona |first=Patrick |title=Wicked movie soundtrack: All the songs featured in Part One |url=https://www.radiotimes.com/movies/wicked-movie-soundtrack-part-1/ |magazine=[[Radio Times]] |access-date=December 1, 2024 |date=December 1, 2024 |archive-date=December 3, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241203233557/https://www.radiotimes.com/movies/wicked-movie-soundtrack-part-1/ |url-status=live}}
* {{Cite magazine |last=Cremona |first=Patrick |date=November 17, 2025 |title=''Wicked: For Good'' soundtrack – all the songs in Part Two including original compositions |url=https://www.radiotimes.com/movies/wicked-for-good-soundtrack/ |access-date=November 21, 2025 |magazine=Radio Times |archive-date=November 18, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251118213655/https://www.radiotimes.com/movies/wicked-for-good-soundtrack/ |url-status=live}}</ref> Both albums received positive reviews and debuted at number two on the ''Billboard'' 200 with 139,000 and 122,000 units, tying for the highest debut for a soundtrack to a [[stage-to-film adaptation]].<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Willman |first=Chris |date=November 23, 2024 |title='Wicked: The Soundtrack' Album Review: Stephen Schwartz's World-Beating Song Score Gets Its Due, And So Do the Divas Who Deliver It |url=https://variety.com/2024/music/album-reviews/wicked-soundtrack-album-review-stephen-schwartz-songs-score-ariana-grande-cynthia-erivo-1236219164/ |access-date=November 24, 2024 |magazine=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] |archive-date=November 23, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241123235133/https://variety.com/2024/music/album-reviews/wicked-soundtrack-album-review-stephen-schwartz-songs-score-ariana-grande-cynthia-erivo-1236219164/ |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine |last=Evans |first=Greg |title='Wicked' Soundtrack Debuts At No. 2 On Billboard 200 Chart, Making History For Broadway-To-Film Adaptations |url=https://deadline.com/2024/12/wicked-soundtrack-billboard-chart-1236191273/ |magazine=[[Deadline Hollywood]] |access-date=December 2, 2024 |date=December 2, 2024 |archive-date=December 3, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241203013357/https://deadline.com/2024/12/wicked-soundtrack-billboard-chart-1236191273/ |url-status=live}}
* {{Cite magazine |last=Caulfield |first=Keith |date=December 2, 2025 |title='Wicked: For Good' Flies Into Top 10 on 7 Billboard Charts |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/chart-beat/wicked-for-good-soundtrack-top-10-seven-billboard-charts-1236126945/ |access-date=December 3, 2025 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |archive-date=December 3, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251203002228/https://www.billboard.com/music/chart-beat/wicked-for-good-soundtrack-top-10-seven-billboard-charts-1236126945/ |url-status=live}}</ref> Grande and her co-star Erivo's rendition of "[[Defying Gravity (song)|Defying Gravity]]" won Best Pop Duo/Group Performance at the [[68th Annual Grammy Awards]].<ref name="grammys2026">{{Cite web |url=https://pitchfork.com/news/ariana-grande-cynthia-erivo-win-best-pop-duo-group-performance-2026-grammys/ |title=Ariana Grande and Cynthia Erivo Win Best Pop Duo/Group Performance at 2026 Grammys |date=February 1, 2026 |access-date=February 2, 2026 |website=Pitchfork |last=Green |first=Walden |first2=Alex |last2=Suskind}}</ref> To promote the ''Wicked'' films, Grande hosted ''Saturday Night Live'' on [[Saturday Night Live season 50#ep971|October 12, 2024]], and [[Saturday Night Live season 51#ep997|December 20, 2025]].<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Longeretta |first=Emily |date=March 10, 2024 |title='SNL': Ariana Grande Previews 'Wicked' Riff After Singing Medley of Hits by Taylor Swift, Jennifer Lopez and More With Bowen Yang |url=https://variety.com/2024/tv/news/snl-ariana-grande-wicked-riff-bowen-yang-skit-video-1235936464/ |access-date=October 10, 2024 |magazine=Variety |archive-date=December 17, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241217132335/https://variety.com/2024/tv/news/snl-ariana-grande-wicked-riff-bowen-yang-skit-video-1235936464/ |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Vasquez |first=Zach |date=December 21, 2025 |title=Saturday Night Live: Ariana Grande Returns to Host a Blockbuster Episode |url=https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2025/dec/21/saturday-night-live-ariana-grande-cher-bowen-yang/ |access-date=December 22, 2025 |work=The Guardian}}</ref> Her 2024 episode drew the show's highest ratings since May 2021, at the time, and became its most-watched episode on [[Peacock (streaming service)|Peacock]] and across social media;<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Shanfeld |first=Ethan |date=October 16, 2024 |title=With Ariana Grande, 'SNL' Scores Most-Watched Episode Since Elon Musk Hosted in 2021 |url=https://variety.com/2024/music/news/ariana-grande-snl-episode-highest-ratings-elon-musk-1236180125/ |access-date=October 18, 2024 |magazine=Variety}}</ref> the 2025 episode was [[Saturday Night Live season 51|season 51]]'s highest-rated and ''SNL''{{'}}s most-watched holiday episode since 2020.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Hailu |first=Selome |date=December 24, 2025 |title=Bowen Yang's 'SNL' Exit Is Most-Watched Episode in a Year |url=https://variety.com/2025/tv/news/bowen-yang-snl-exit-ratings-1236617144/ |access-date=December 27, 2025 |magazine=Variety}}</ref> She and Erivo opened the [[97th Academy Awards]] with a medley of "[[Over the Rainbow]]", "[[Home (The Wiz song)|Home]]", and "Defying Gravity".<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Romano |first=Nick |date=March 2, 2025 |title=''Wicked'' Stars Ariana Grande and Cynthia Erivo Open 2025 Oscars with Gravity-Defying ''Wizard of Oz'' Medley |url=https://ew.com/ariana-grande-cynthia-erivo-oscars-2025-wizard-of-oz-medley-11689202/ |access-date=March 3, 2025 |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]}}</ref> It was reported in October 2025 that Grande was set to appear in the [[American Horror Story season 13|thirteenth season]] of the horror anthology series ''[[American Horror Story]]'';<ref>{{Cite web |last=Omotade |first=Lade |date=April 10, 2026 |title=Epic 13-Part Horror Series Drops First Look at New Fantasy Sequel |url=https://collider.com/ryan-murphy-fantasy-series-american-horror-story-season-13-sarah-paulson-jessica-lange-first-images-release-window-september-2026/ |access-date=April 13, 2025 |website=[[Collider (website)|Collider]]}}</ref> her involvement was later canceled due to scheduling conflicts.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Cordero |first=Rosy |date=July 10, 2026 |title=Ariana Grande Will Not Be In 'American Horror Story' Season 13 |url=https://deadline.com/2026/07/ariana-grande-exits-ahs-season-13-1236979292 |access-date=July 10, 2026 |work=[[Deadline Hollywood]] |publisher=[[Penske Media Corporation]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |last=VanHoose |first=Benjamin |date=July 10, 2026 |title=Ariana Grande No Longer Starring in American Horror Story Season 13 |url=https://people.com/ariana-grande-no-longer-american-horror-story-12016334 |access-date=July 10, 2026 |magazine=[[People (magazine)|People]] |publisher=[[People Inc.]] |issn=0093-7673 |oclc=794712888}}</ref> In November 2025, Grande appeared in the special ''[[Wicked: One Wonderful Night]]'', performing music from the ''Wicked'' films alongside the cast;<ref>{{Cite news |last=Campione |first=Katie |date=October 22, 2025 |title='Wicked: One Wonderful Night' First-Look Photos Tease Swankified NBC Broadcast Special Featuring Cynthia Erivo, Ariana Grande & More |url=https://deadline.com/2025/10/wicked-one-wonderful-night-first-look-photos-cynthia-ariana-1236594175/ |access-date=November 19, 2025 |work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> a live album of the special was released in tandem with the broadcast.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Brandle |first=Lars |date=November 11, 2025 |title=Like Magic, 'Wicked: One Wonderful Night (Live)' Has Arrived: Stream It Now |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/pop/wicked-one-wonderful-night-live-stream-1236107430/ |access-date=November 19, 2025 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref> For her and Erivo's role as principal performers and co-hosts in the special, they were nominated alongside the producers for [[Primetime Emmy Award for Outstanding Variety Special (Pre-Recorded)|Outstanding Variety Special (Pre-Recorded)]] at the [[78th Primetime Creative Arts Emmy Awards]].<ref name="wickedemmys">{{cite web |author=<!--Not stated--> |url=https://www.televisionacademy.com/shows/wicked-one-wonderful-night |title=Wicked: One Wonderful Night |publisher=[[Academy of Television Arts & Sciences]] |access-date=October 12, 2026}}</ref>
[[File:Ariana Grande Eternal Sunshine Tour on Stage.jpg|thumb|Grande at [[the Eternal Sunshine Tour]] in 2026]]
In May 2026, Grande released a special edition of her album ''Dangerous Woman'' for its tenth anniversary, containing a new track, "Knew Better Part Two".<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mickles |first=Kiana |date=May 20, 2026 |title=Ariana Grande Drops ''Dangerous Woman'' Outtake "Knew Better Part Two" |url=https://pitchfork.com/news/ariana-grande-releases-fan-favorite-single-knew-better-part-two/ |access-date=May 22, 2026 |website=[[Pitchfork (website)|Pitchfork]]}}</ref> She then headlined [[the Eternal Sunshine Tour]], her first concert tour since 2019, spanning 41 arena shows across North America and England, between June and September 2026.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Dailey |first=Hannah |date=September 16, 2025 |title=Ariana Grande Unveils Final Round of 2026 Eternal Sunshine Tour Dates, Adds 5 London Shows |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/pop/ariana-grande-final-eternal-sunshine-2026-tour-dates-london-1236067300/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250916174436/https://www.billboard.com/music/pop/ariana-grande-final-eternal-sunshine-2026-tour-dates-london-1236067300/ |archive-date=September 16, 2025 |access-date=September 16, 2025 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |issn=0006-2510 |oclc=732913734}}</ref> The tour was met with critical acclaim for its production, storytelling, and Grande's vocals. It grossed $107.9{{nbsp}}million and sold over 638,000 tickets, becoming her second-highest-grossing tour.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Frankenberg |first=Eric |date=September 2, 2026 |title=Ariana Grande's Eternal Sunshine Tour Surpasses $100 Million in Grosses |url=https://www.billboard.com/pro/ariana-grande-eternal-sunshine-tour-gross-100-million/ |access-date=September 5, 2026 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref> Grande's eighth studio album, ''[[Petal (album)|Petal]]'', was released on July 31, 2026, and is her first album under the imprint Babydoll Music, which she founded. All her future releases will be owned by Babydoll and licensed to Republic Records.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Havens |first=Lyndsey |date=April 30, 2026 |title=Ariana Grande's Babydoll Music, Explained |url=https://www.billboard.com/pro/ariana-grande-petal-album-release-what-is-babydoll-music |url-access=subscription |access-date=June 25, 2026 |work=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |publisher=[[Penske Media Corporation]] |issn=0006-2510 |oclc=732913734}}</ref> Revolving around themes of romance, self-worth, fame, and public scrutiny, it delves into atmospheric production and an electronic-R&B soundscape.<ref>{{cite news |last=Hawthorne |first=Katie |url=https://www.theguardian.com/music/2026/jul/31/ariana-grande-petal-album-review |title=Ariana Grande: ''Petal'' Review – Calm, Controlled Anger at Exes, Fans and the Media |newspaper=[[The Guardian]] |date=July 31, 2026 |access-date=October 12, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260801023646/https://www.theguardian.com/music/2026/jul/31/ariana-grande-petal-album-review |archive-date=August 1, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |author-link=Neil McCormick |last=McCormick |first=Neil |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/music/news/ariana-grandes-temper-tantrum-being-attacked-butterfly/ |title=Ariana Grande's Temper Tantrum Is like Being Attacked by a Lovely Butterfly |newspaper=[[The Daily Telegraph]] |date=July 31, 2026 |access-date=October 12, 2026 |archive-date=July 31, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260731152809/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/music/news/ariana-grandes-temper-tantrum-being-attacked-butterfly/ |url-status=live}}</ref> It received generally favorable reviews from critics.<ref>{{cite web |title=Petal by Ariana Grande Reviews and Tracks |url=https://www.metacritic.com/music/petal/ariana-grande |website=Metacritic |access-date=August 6, 2026}}</ref> ''Petal'' debuted atop the ''Billboard'' 200 with 295,000 units, marking Grande's seventh number-one album and the second-largest sales week of her career. With 168,000 pure sales (comprising 96,000 vinyl sales), it was her second-largest pure sales debut and largest week in vinyl sales.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Caulfield |first=Keith |date=August 9, 2026 |title=Ariana Grande Achieves Seventh No. 1 Album on ''Billboard'' 200 With 'petal' |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/chart-beat/ariana-grande-petal-number-one-billboard-200-chart-1236312334/https://www.billboard.com/music/chart-beat/ariana-grande-petal-number-one-billboard-200-chart-1236312334/ |access-date=August 10, 2026 |magazine=Billboard}}</ref> It topped the charts in nineteen other countries, becoming her sixth number-one in Australia and the UK<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Brandle |first=Lars |date=August 7, 2026 |title=Ariana Grande's 'Petal' Drops In at No. 1 In Australia |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/chart-beat/ariana-grande-petal-no-1-australia-1236311390/ |access-date=August 10, 2026 |magazine=Billboard}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Smith |first=Thomas |date=August 8, 2026 |title=Ariana Grande Earns Her Sixth Consecutive U.K. No. 1 Album With 'Petal' |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/chart-beat/ariana-grande-petal-number-1-uk-albums-chart-1236311517/ |access-date=August 10, 2026 |magazine=Billboard}}</ref> and her first number-one in France and Germany.<ref>{{Cite web |date=August 7, 2026 |title=Ariana Grande tops German charts for first time with new album 'petal' |url=https://www.yahoo.com/entertainment/music/articles/ariana-grande-tops-german-charts-161831977.html |access-date=August 9, 2026 |publisher=[[Deutsche Presse-Agentur]] |via=[[Yahoo! Entertainment]]}}</ref> The album was preceded by the lead single, "[[Hate That I Made You Love Me]]", on May 29;<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Dailey |first=Hannah |date=May 8, 2026 |title=Ariana Grande Announces 'Petal' Lead Single & Release Date: 'One of My Favorite Songs I'll Ever Write' |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/music-news/ariana-grande-petal-lead-single-release-date-1236242721/ |access-date=May 11, 2026 |magazine=Billboard}}</ref> debuting atop the ''Billboard'' Hot 100 and UK singles chart, it marked Grande's tenth US and eighth UK number-one single, extending her record for the most number-one debuts as a woman in the UK.<ref name="htimylm1" /><ref>{{cite magazine |last=Smith |first=Thomas |date=June 5, 2026 |title=Ariana Grande's 'Hate That I Made You Love Me' Debuts at No. 1 on U.K. Singles Chart |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/chart-beat/ariana-grande-hate-that-i-made-you-love-me-number-1-uk-single-1236265067/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260606140646/https://www.billboard.com/music/chart-beat/ariana-grande-hate-that-i-made-you-love-me-number-1-uk-single-1236265067/ |archive-date=June 6, 2026 |access-date=June 6, 2026 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref> It also became her eleventh number-one on the US Pop Airplay chart,<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Trust |first=Gary |date=September 4, 2026 |title=Ariana Grande's 'Hate That I Made You Love Me' Hits No. 1 on Pop Airplay Chart |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/chart-beat/ariana-grande-hate-that-i-made-you-love-me-number-1-pop-airplay-1236334350/ |access-date=September 5, 2026 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref> her first number-one on the [[Adult Pop Airplay]] chart,<ref>{{Cite magazine |title=Ariana Grande Chart History (Adult Pop Songs) |url=https://www.billboard.com/artist/ariana-grande/chart-history/atf/ |access-date=October 12, 2026 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref> and topped the ''Billboard'' Global 200 and Global Excl. US charts for three and two weeks, her fourth and fifth chart-toppers on each tally.<ref>*{{cite magazine |last=Trust |first=Gary |title=Ariana Grande's 'Hate That I Made You Love Me' Launches at No. 1 on Both ''Billboard'' Global Charts |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/chart-beat/ariana-grande-hate-that-i-made-you-love-me-number-1-global-1236267311/ |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |access-date=June 9, 2026 |date=June 8, 2026}}
*{{cite magazine |last=Trust |first=Gary |title=A Whole 'Knew' Worldwide No. 1: Taylor Swift Debuts Atop Billboard Global 200 Chart |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/chart-beat/taylor-swift-i-knew-it-i-knew-you-global-charts-june-20-1236273186/ |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |access-date=June 15, 2026 |date=June 15, 2026}}
*{{Cite magazine |last=Trust |first=Gary |date=July 6, 2026 |title=Shakira & Burna Boy's World Cup Song 'Dai Dai' Scores Second Week at No. 1 on Global Excl. U.S. Chart |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/chart-beat/shakira-burna-boy-dai-dai-global-charts-second-week-1236288306/ |access-date=July 7, 2026 |magazine=Billboard}}</ref> ''Petal''{{'}}s [[Petal (song)|title track]] accompanied its release as the second single and reached the top three and top five on the Global 200 and Hot 100 charts.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Trust |first=Gary |date=August 10, 2026 |title=Ella Langley's 'Choosin' Texas' No. 1 on Hot 100 for 17th Week, Ariana Grande Has Two in Top 5 |url=https://www.billboard.com/lists/ella-langley-choosin-texas-hot-100-number-one-17-weeks/ |access-date=August 10, 2026 |magazine=Billboard}}</ref><ref name="petalglobal200">{{cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/chart-beat/ariana-grande-shakira-burna-boy-global-charts-aug-15-1236312872/|title=Ariana Grande Has Half of the ''Billboard'' Global 200's Top 10, Led by 'Hate That I Made You Love Me' at No. 1|last=Trust|first=Gary|magazine=Billboard|date=August 10, 2026|access-date=August 10, 2026}}</ref> All twelve tracks from the album charted within the top 40 of the Hot 100;<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Zellner |first=Xander |date=August 10, 2026 |title=Ariana Grande Charts All 12 Songs From 'petal' on Hot 100, Surpasses 100 Career Entries |url=https://www.billboard.com/music/chart-beat/ariana-grande-charts-petal-songs-hot-100-1236312898/ |access-date=August 11, 2026 |magazine=Billboard}}</ref> Grande occupied five of the top-ten spots on the Global 200.<ref name="petalglobal200" />

She was set to star in the 2027 [[Barbican Centre]] production of the stage musical ''[[Sunday in the Park with George]]'' opposite her ''Wicked'' co-star [[Jonathan Bailey]];<ref>{{cite news |last1=Bernabe |first1=Angeline Jane|last2=Dresdale |first2=Andrea |url=https://abcnews.com/GMA/Culture/wicked-stars-ariana-grande-jonathan-bailey-reunite-sondheim/story?id=129211512 |title='Wicked' stars Ariana Grande, Jonathan Bailey to reunite for Sondheim musical revival |publisher=[[ABC News (United States)|ABC News]] |date=January 14, 2026 |access-date=August 3, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260803153140/https://abcnews.com/GMA/Culture/wicked-stars-ariana-grande-jonathan-bailey-reunite-sondheim/story?id=129211512 |archive-date=August 3, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> however, her involvement was canceled in August 2026, which a representative described as part of a plan to "[take] a step back from visibility" following the Eternal Sunshine Tour.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Garner |first=Glenn |title=Ariana Grande Exits West End's 'Sunday in the Park with George' |url=https://deadline.com/2026/08/ariana-grande-exits-west-end-sunday-in-the-park-with-george-1237015542 |work=[[Deadline Hollywood]] |date=August 2, 2026 |access-date=August 2, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260802200354/https://deadline.com/2026/08/ariana-grande-exits-west-end-sunday-in-the-park-with-george-1237015542 |archive-date=August 2, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Rice |first=Nicholas |title=Ariana Grande Is 'Taking a Step Back from Visibility' After Tour as Public Scrutiny Intensifies: Rep (Exclusive) |url=https://people.com/ariana-grande-taking-step-back-after-tour-amid-public-health-scrutiny-rep-exclusive-12032395 |magazine=[[People (magazine)|People]] |date=August 2, 2026 |access-date=August 2, 2026 |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20260802200830/https://people.com/ariana-grande-taking-step-back-after-tour-amid-public-health-scrutiny-rep-exclusive-12032395 |archive-date=August 2, 2026 |url-status=live }}</ref> Grande's upcoming film projects include ''[[Focker-in-Law]]'' (2026)<ref>{{Cite web |last=Hughes |first=William |date=April 15, 2026 |title=It's Ariana Grande's turn to Fock things up in the Focker-In-Law trailer |url=https://www.avclub.com/focker-in-law-trailer-ariana-grande-ben-stiller-robert-de-niro/ |access-date=May 23, 2026 |website=[[The A.V. Club]]}}</ref> and an animated film adaptation of [[Dr. Seuss]]'s 1990 book ''[[Oh, the Places You'll Go!]]'' (2028).<ref>{{Cite news |last=Grobar |first=Matt |date=July 15, 2025 |title=Ariana Grande & Josh Gad Join Warner Bros Pictures Animation's 'Oh, The Places You'll Go!' |url=https://deadline.com/2025/07/oh-the-places-youll-go-movie-casts-ariana-grande-josh-gad-1236458241/ |access-date=July 17, 2025 |work=Deadline Hollywood}}</ref>

== Artistry ==
=== Influences ===
{{Multiple image
| footer            = Grande credits [[Mariah Carey]] (left) and [[Whitney Houston]] (right) as her major vocal influences.
| image1            = Mariah Carey13 Edwards Dec 1998.jpg
| width1            = 155
| alt1              = Mariah Carey
| image2            = Whitney Houston Welcome Home Heroes 1 cropped.jpg
| width2            = 155
